<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2013/Welsh-Farm.jpg" alt="This plein air painting was done in an impressionistic style" width="500" height="291" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Welsh Farm. &nbsp;Oil on linen. &nbsp;Approx 6"x10". 2013. For sale at Bluemont Fair.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I painted this early in the morning and was facing the sun more than I prefer. The combination of sunlight and humidity helped to suppress the greens in the tree line and gave me the chance to bring out the violets and yellows in the field. &nbsp;Before starting the painting I walked through the field and found that most of the purple vegetation was actually mint growing wild.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I made the sky area a pale yellow to try and approximate the warm bright light. &nbsp;The middle and forground are built up from strokes of thick paint.</p>